# foodpanda-scraper — copy to .env next to the scripts and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   python3 env_config.py        # prints what was picked up, WITHOUT secrets
#
# Credentials belong here and never on a command line: a secret in argv is
# readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in shell history.
# `.env` is in .gitignore; keep it that way.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   an explicit flag  ->  an exported environment variable  ->  .env  ->  default
#
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER. Anything still carrying `{...}` braces
# is treated as unset, so a copied example is never sent to an API as if it
# were a key — the alternative is a 401 a long way from its cause.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2Captcha — one key, four separately billed products
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captcha solving, the Scraping Browser API, proxies and fingerprints all sit
# behind this one key: https://2captcha.com
#
# WHAT THIS KEY IS WORTH HERE: the Scraping Browser API, the fingerprint
# client and the Scraper API were all run end to end against foodpanda on
# 2026-09-15 and all three work. The captcha SOLVER is the one that is not
# worth buying for this site — read on.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE BUYING THE SOLVER FOR THIS SITE. foodpanda's refusal is
# PerimeterX, and when PerimeterX renders a captcha at all it renders
# reCAPTCHA **Enterprise** — measured on four denial documents across two
# country sites, all of them loading
# https://www.google.com/recaptcha/enterprise.js and none of them loading
# recaptcha/api.js. This project implements reCAPTCHA v2 and v3 and NOT the
# enterprise method, so it reports such a page as `blocked` and never attempts
# a solve. Your key is not charged for it, and it would not help if it were.
#
# What DOES clear a refusal here, measured: a fresh browser session and a
# slower request rate. What the paid products buy is volume from many
# addresses and a specific exit country — which is what a multi-page run on
# this site actually runs out of.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Scraping Browser API — a remote browser over CDP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   country-{cc}   picks the exit country. Worth matching to the country site
#                  you are scraping: an exit in the site's own country is the
#                  most convincing address available
#   pid-{id}       a profile with persistent cookies, ONE live connection
#                  each — reuse pids rather than minting one per run
#
# --concurrency above 1 is refused with --cdp-endpoint, because a profile
# allows one live connection and workers would collide (profile_locked). Use
# several pids, one run each.
#
# MEASURED against foodpanda on 2026-09-15, and it is the best path this
# repo has: three pages of a real area listing returned 144 vendors with
# status `complete`, zero refusals, zero retries, in 29 seconds. The same
# three pages from an unproxied residential address needed five attempts on
# page 3 and about seven minutes.
#
# It also sidesteps the two proxy traps below entirely, because the remote
# browser brings its own exit.
#
# NOTE: selenium_scraper.py cannot use this. chromedriver's `debuggerAddress`
# takes a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password; Playwright and
# pyppeteer authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work fine.
FOODPANDA_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-pk-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A proxy exit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read as a single exit, or use --proxy-file for a pool.
#
# What a proxy is and is NOT for on this site:
#
#  * It is NOT needed to be served at all. A plain residential address with an
#    ordinary headful Chromium was served by ten of the eleven country sites
#    on 2026-09-15, with no proxy and no key.
#
#  * It IS the thing that makes a MULTI-PAGE run work. The refusal rate here
#    is a function of request rate from one address: 10 of 30 navigations
#    served over a 20-minute sweep from a single exit, and a three-page run
#    from an already-warm address had page 2 refused on all five attempts. A
#    pool spreads that; --delay is the cheaper lever and should be raised
#    first.
#
#  * Pick the site's own country where you can. `ap.proxy.2captcha.com` is
#    the regional gateway for the Asian sites this brand operates.
#
#  * TWO THINGS TO CHECK BEFORE YOU BLAME THE SITE, both measured on a real
#    credential on 2026-09-15 and both explained in TROUBLESHOOTING.md:
#
#      1. Does the zone answer `407` to an UNAUTHENTICATED CONNECT? Chromium
#         sends one first and waits for that challenge; a gateway that stalls
#         instead hangs every page load with ERR_TIMED_OUT at ~30s, to every
#         destination, while `requests` through the same credential works
#         perfectly. IP WHITELISTING avoids the handshake entirely and is the
#         recommended fix.
#      2. Does the zone rotate per request? Four requests from four different
#         addresses is normal for a rotating zone and unusable for a browser.
#         Pin it with `-session-{id}-sessTime-{minutes}` in the USERNAME.
#
# Note Selenium cannot authenticate a proxy at all (--proxy-server takes an
# address only). 2Captcha's IP-whitelist mode is the way around that:
# whitelist your address, ask /proxy/generate_white_list_connections for
# connections, and you get one `host:port` per exit with no credentials in
# them at all.
FOODPANDA_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@ap.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A default URL, so a run needs no --url
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any listing on any of the eleven country sites:
#
#   area listing   https://www.foodpanda.pk/city/lahore/area/gulberg
#                  — the one that paginates, with ?page=N addresses the site
#                    publishes itself
#   city listing   https://www.foodpanda.sg/city/singapore
#                  — one page of curated vendors, no pagination
#   home page      https://www.foodpanda.my/
#                  — a curated set, scrolled rather than paged
#
# Not supported, and refused with the reason: /restaurant/{code}/{slug} vendor
# pages (every attempt was answered 403), /city and /city/{city}/area
# directories (no vendor tiles on them), and foodpanda.com (a country picker).
FOODPANDA_URL=https://www.foodpanda.pk/city/lahore/area/gulberg
